{
  "_comment": "Manifest-entry attributes specific to @shexjs/neighborhood-sparql, stacked onto ../../doc/webapp-manifest-context.jsonld's core (see doc/manifest-vocabulary.md for the survey this came out of). A manifest entry that names this neighborhood (neighborhood: sparql, a core attribute) writes this backend's own parameters under the sparql: prefix, e.g. sparql:endpoint, rather than bare `endpoint` -- so it can never collide with the same-shaped attribute another backend defines. This is a tentative home: a SPARQL endpoint isn't specific to ShEx or to shex.js, so other RDF tooling may want this vocabulary too. If a better shared home turns up (a SPARQL-protocol-adjacent namespace, say), this prefix should point there instead.",

  "@context": {
    "sparql": "http://shex.io/neighborhoods/sparql#",
    "sparql:endpoint": {"@id": "sparql:endpoint", "@type": "@id"}
  }
}
